{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Dissolving and recovering substances","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ff","foreground":"#1d3557","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-term","content":"Dissolving"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-exp","content":"When a solid mixes into a liquid and seems to disappear. The mixture is then called a solution."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-term","content":"Solution"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-exp","content":"A mixture made when a solid dissolves in a liquid. The solid is still there, but you cannot see it."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c3-pic","picto":"cup"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these will dissolve in water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Sugar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Pebbles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What is the name of the liquid in a salt solution?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Solvent","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Crystal","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Is sand more likely to dissolve in water, or to stay as grains?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Dissolve","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Stay as grains","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c6-pic","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Your class has salty water in a dish. You want the salt back. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Leave it in the sun to evaporate","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Pour it down the sink","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The water slowly turns to vapour and leaves the salt behind as white crystals. Well done!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"The salt goes down the drain with the water. You have lost it. Try a different way next time."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"What is the best way to get a dissolved solid back from its solution?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Filter it","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Let the water evaporate","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Shake it hard","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-h","content":"Well done! You finished the quiz."},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"You now know how some materials dissolve in liquid to make a solution, and how to get the solid back out."}],"actions":[]}}
